latin typeface="Comic Sans MS" pitchFamily="66" charset="0"/></a:rPr><a:t>Crystal</a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" dirty="0"><a:latin typeface="Comic Sans MS" pitchFamily="66" charset="0"/></a:rPr><a:t> – a large, orderly arrangement of atoms or molecules in neat rows.</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" u="sng" dirty="0"><a:latin typeface="Comic Sans MS" pitchFamily="66" charset="0"/></a:endParaRPr></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" u="sng" dirty="0"><a:latin typeface="Comic Sans MS" pitchFamily="66" charset="0"/></a:rPr><a:t>Solvent </a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" dirty="0"><a:latin typeface="Comic Sans MS" pitchFamily="66" charset="0"/></a:rPr><a:t>– a liquid (like water) that you dissolve stuff in.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" u="sng" dirty="0"><a:latin typeface="Comic Sans MS" pitchFamily="66" charset="0"/></a:rPr><a:t>Solute </a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" dirty="0"><a:latin typeface="Comic Sans MS" pitchFamily="66" charset="0"/></a:rPr><a:t>– a solid (like sugar) that you dissolve in the solvent.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" u="sng" dirty="0"><a:latin typeface="Comic Sans MS" pitchFamily="66" charset="0"/></a:rPr><a:t>Solution</a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" dirty="0"><a:latin typeface="Comic Sans MS" pitchFamily="66" charset="0"/></a:rPr><a:t> – the mixture of solvent and solute (like sugar water).</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" u="sng" dirty="0"><a:latin typeface="Comic Sans MS" pitchFamily="66" charset="0"/></a:rPr><a:t>Saturated solution</a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" dirty="0"><a:latin typeface="Comic Sans MS" pitchFamily="66" charset="0"/></a:rPr><a:t> – a solution (like sugar in water) that can’t hold any more solute.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" u="sng" dirty="0"><a:latin typeface="Comic Sans MS" pitchFamily="66" charset="0"/></a:rPr><a:t>Supersaturated solution</a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" dirty="0"><a:latin typeface="Comic Sans MS" pitchFamily="66" charset="0"/></a:rPr><a:t> – a solution that has been heated and holds more solute (like sugar) than it can at room temperature.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" u="sng" dirty="0"><a:latin typeface="Comic Sans MS" pitchFamily="66" charset="0"/></a:rPr><a:t>Nucleation</a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" dirty="0"><a:latin typeface="Comic Sans MS" pitchFamily="66" charset="0"/></a:rPr><a:t> – the process in which a sugar molecule (solute) comes out of the sugar water solution and sticks to the sugar crystals on the string.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:endParaRPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" dirty="0"><a:latin typeface="Comic Sans MS" pitchFamily="66" charset="0"/></a:endParaRPr></a:p><a:p><a:endParaRPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" dirty="0"><a:latin typeface="Comic Sans MS" pitchFamily="66" charset="0"/></a:endParaRPr></a:p><a:p><a:endParaRPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" dirty="0"><a:latin typeface="Comic Sans MS" pitchFamily="66" charset="0"/></a:endParaRPr></a:p><a:p><a:endParaRPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" dirty="0"><a:latin typeface="Comic Sans MS" pitchFamily="66" charset="0"/></a:endParaRPr></a:p><a:p><a:endParaRPr lang="en-US" sz="2200" dirty="0"><a:latin typeface="Comic Sans MS" pitchFamily="66" charset="0"/></a:endParaRPr></a:p><a:p><a:pPr lvl="8"/><a:endParaRPr lang="en-US" sz="1000" dirty="0"><a:latin typeface="Comic Sans MS" pitchFamily="66" charset="0"/></a:endParaRPr></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="1026" name="AutoShape 2" descr="Image result for image of copper"/><p:cNvSpPr><a:spLocks noChangeAspect="1" noChangeArrowheads="1"/></p:cNvSpPr><p:nvPr/></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr bwMode="auto"><a:xfrm><a:off x="155575" y="-144463"/><a:ext cx="304800" cy="304801"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:noFill/></p:spPr><p:txBody><a:bodyPr vert="horz" wrap="square" lIns="91440" tIns="45720" rIns="91440"